---
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import TextSection from '../components/TextSection.astro';
import { hiddenFunctions } from '../data/hidden-functions.ts';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';

const functions = Object.values(hiddenFunctions);
---

<Site
  title="The doorman fallacy"
  current="idea"
  description="Rory Sutherland's doorman fallacy: judging a job by its most visible task, and replacing the task, can remove the work nobody wrote down."
>
  <div class="page">
    <PageHead
      title="The doorman fallacy"
      lead="Judging a job by its most visible task, and replacing the task, can remove the work nobody wrote down."
    />

    <TextSection id="story-title" title="The story">
      <p>
        Rory Sutherland tells it in his book <i>Alchemy</i> (2019). A hotel hires consultants to cut costs.
        They describe the doorman&rsquo;s job as opening the door, and an automatic door does that for less.
        So the doorman goes.
      </p>
      <p>
        The door still opens. But the doorman also greeted regular guests by name, found taxis in the rain,
        kept an eye on who came in, and told every arriving guest that this was a hotel that looked after
        people. None of that was in the job description, so none of it was counted when the decision was
        made. Its cost turns up later, somewhere else.
      </p>
      <p class="t-small ink-2">
        The idea and the story are Rory Sutherland&rsquo;s. <i>Alchemy: The Surprising Power of Ideas That
        Don&rsquo;t Make Sense</i>, 2019.
      </p>
    </TextSection>

    <TextSection id="now-title" title="Why it matters now">
      <p>
        AI can now do many visible tasks well: answer the customer&rsquo;s question, write the product text,
        screen the application. When a role is described by its visible task, the case for replacing it looks
        simple. The savings are counted on the task. The hidden work is not counted, because nobody listed
        it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site&rsquo;s view is practical. Use AI where it does the job. Before deciding, count everything
        the person did.
      </p>
    </TextSection>

    <TextSection id="hidden-title" title="The hidden work">
      <p>Six kinds of work that disappear without being missed at first.</p>
      <ul slot="wide" class="grid columns columns--3">
        {
          functions.map(({ label, meaning }) => (
            <li class="ruled">
              <h3 class="t-title">{label}</h3>
              <p class="t-lead ink-2">{meaning}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </TextSection>

    <div class="idea-close grid">
      <div class="idea-close__photo">
        <Photo id="portrait" sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 33vw, 100vw" />
      </div>
      <ul class="idea-close__links t-lead">
        <li><a href="/ledger">See what happened in practice</a></li>
        <li><a href="/checks/your-hidden-job">Before the decision: two printable guides</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Site>

<style>
  .idea-close {
    row-gap: var(--space-12);
    align-items: end;
    padding-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-24);
  }

  .idea-close__photo,
  .idea-close__links {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .idea-close__links {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  @media (width >= 56rem) {
    .idea-close__photo {
      grid-column: 1 / span 4;
    }

    .idea-close__links {
      grid-column: 6 / span 7;
    }
  }
</style>
